diff -ruN phase23_base/PLANNING_VECTOR_FUSION.md phase23_work/PLANNING_VECTOR_FUSION.md
--- phase23_base/PLANNING_VECTOR_FUSION.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ phase23_work/PLANNING_VECTOR_FUSION.md	2026-08-05 22:26:17.291872431 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Planning vector fusion and gated OSM repair
+
+Phase 23 promotes selected Phase 22 planning-drawing vectors into the existing planning-authority conflict engine. Promotion is not automatic acceptance: every feature still passes status, confidence, geometry overlap, displacement and ambiguity checks before it can alter the normalized map.
+
+## Modes
+
+- `off`: do not evaluate or promote planning vectors.
+- `review`: run all preparation gates and write decisions, but do not expose candidates to map fusion.
+- `gated`: require a declared reusable/open document licence. Implemented/as-built geometry may fill gaps; approved-only geometry may repair a matching OSM feature but cannot create a missing feature.
+- `private`: permits unknown-licence portal evidence only for explicitly private-use-restricted builds. Every accepted feature is marked non-redistributable in the evidence and source metadata.
+- `authoritative`: permits approved layouts to fill gaps as an intentional future/approved-layout build policy. This should not be used for an as-built reconstruction.
+
+## Semantic promotion
+
+The first release automatically supports:
+
+- access path centrelines and access surfaces;
+- ride centrelines and ride footprints;
+- building footprints from floor plans;
+- landscape polygons and boundaries;
+- drainage lines;
+- lighting areas and layouts.
+
+Ambiguous site-plan linework, unknown polygons, terrain/drainage polygons and page/detail noise remain withheld because their meaning cannot be inferred safely from geometry alone.
+
+## Current-layout rules
+
+Implemented, existing and as-built records can add missing features or replace inaccurate OSM geometry.
+
+Approved-only records in `gated` mode are target-only: an OSM feature must already exist within the configured match distance. This allows an approved drawing to correct a known path or footprint without assuming that every approved proposal was built.
+
+Refused, withdrawn, pending, superseded, invalid, expired and draft evidence is never promoted.
+
+## Metadata preservation
+
+When a planning vector replaces OSM, the engine retains useful OSM evidence that the drawing does not provide, including names, tags, path surface/width semantics, subtype and measured height/elevation evidence. The planning document reference, hash, licence, georeferencing error and replacement metrics remain attached to the resulting feature.
+
+## Outputs
+
+`planning-vector-fusion.json` contains:
+
+- preparation gates and rejection reasons;
+- private-use restrictions;
+- promoted candidate counts by map kind;
+- planning-authority outcomes;
+- every vector addition, replacement, corroboration and withheld conflict.
+
+The existing `planning-authority-decisions.json` remains the complete authority-level audit.
